From: Lu-Fi <lu-fi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: jz_mac: T33 runs the GMAC clock at 50 MHz like the vendor

The T33 vendor kernel (3.10.14 isvp_goat H20250916a, jz_mii_bus_probe)
calls clk_set_rate(div_gmac, 50000000) (CPM MACCDR); this tree set 25 MHz.
On the JZT33L D61 module (TI DP83825 RMII PHY at address 0) eth0 passed no
traffic at 25 MHz (udhcpc: no lease on a known-good port).

---
 drivers/net/ethernet/ingenic/jz_mac_v13.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/ingenic/jz_mac_v13.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/ingenic/jz_mac_v13.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/ingenic/jz_mac_v13.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/ingenic/jz_mac_v13.c
@@ -2267,7 +2267,12 @@
 		clk_put(clk_gate);
 		goto out_err_alloc;
 	}
-#ifdef CONFIG_FPGA_TEST
+#if defined(CONFIG_FPGA_TEST) || defined(CONFIG_SOC_PRJ008)
+	/*
+	 * T33 (PRJ008) RMII boards: the vendor kernel runs the GMAC divider
+	 * (CPM MACCDR) at 50 MHz, the RMII reference clock. With 25 MHz
+	 * eth0 passes no traffic on the JZT33L module.
+	 */
 	clk_set_rate(clk_div, 50000000);
 #else
 	clk_set_rate(clk_div, 25000000);
